      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T18:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You may be referring to a now-deleted call to obtain the `DawnTextureSpec` off of `TextureInfo`, but that got refactored within https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/882809 in an effort to reduce/eliminate `#ifdef SK_DAWN` from classes used by multiple backends.\n\nAFAICT, the only way to access the needed `YcbcrVkDescriptor` is from a texture\u0027s `DawnTextureInfo`, which is now seemingly expected to be obtained by `TextureInfos::Get[backend]TextureInfo(...)` methods which take in a `TextureInfo` and `[Backend]TextureInfo`(populating the latter).\n\nPlease do LMK if I am missing something more direct. I did consolidate some calls here which cuts down on some definitions, but that\u0027s all.",
      "parentUuid": "fb2f7338_ff829b5f",
      "range": {
